From fbb5f272d540eea4cfa6cf0a202da6e1ecc92dc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:34:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DSMod: read zstd romfs files with ZsDic

TotK keeps almost every romfs file as a zstd frame whose header names a
dictionary from Pack/ZsDic.pack.zs, so romfs:/...zs sources and module
read_romfs paths into them could not be read.

New pure helper src/core/mods/mod_zstd.{h,cpp} (Core::Mods::Zstd::Dicts,
no runtime, no logging): Add() keys a ZSTD_DDict by its dictionary id
and refuses id 0 and duplicates; Decode() wants the zstd magic, a known
content size at or below the cap, a known dictionary when the frame
names one ("unknown zstd dictionary <id>"), and output equal to the
content size.

NxAssetState::Locate gets a zstd branch shaped like the Yaz0 one
(ReadAll, decode capped at MaxWholeRead, VectorVfsFile,
RememberExpanded). A frame naming a dictionary loads the dictionaries
once per source prefix: <prefix>:Pack/ZsDic.pack.zs (plain zstd, never
loads dictionaries itself) -> NX::ParseSarc -> Dicts::Add for every
member ending .zsdic. They are kept in NxAssetState under io_mutex and
cleared by ResetNxAssets; a failed load is remembered with one warning
until then. IsNxAssetSource tests the file name without a trailing .zs,
so X.bntx.zs is an NX source.

core already links zstd::zstd. The ledger lists mod_zstd.{h,cpp} and
the two upstream files 0005 and 0007 edit (sparse_large_vector.cpp,
launch_params.cpp), which duo-touched-ledger.sh --check reported.

